<section class="program-dossier__panel" id="program-panel-ekrp" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="program-tab-ekrp" hidden>
  <header class="program-dossier__masthead">
    <div><p class="research-eyebrow">EKRP / application-profile study</p><h3>Knowledge representation that leaves its conditions of use visible.</h3></div>
    <p>EKRP is a source-only program for exploring readable, provenance-aware knowledge representation before claiming a runtime, query service, or universal vocabulary.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="program-dossier__layout">
    <section><p class="research-eyebrow">Core question</p><strong>How can a record carry source, context, uncertainty, and review state without becoming a black box?</strong><p>The profile treats the document system itself as an inspectable design problem: what belongs together, what stays separate, and what must remain withheld.</p></section>
    <section><p class="research-eyebrow">Primary objects</p><dl><div><dt>Evidence packet</dt><dd>A bounded set of sources, observations, limits, and review questions.</dd></div><div><dt>Projection receipt</dt><dd>A record of what a public transformation preserves and omits.</dd></div><div><dt>Crosswalk</dt><dd>A comparison aid, never a conformance claim by resemblance.</dd></div></dl></section>
  </div>
  <section class="program-dossier__sequence" aria-label="EKRP study sequence"><div><span>01</span><strong>Locate</strong><p>Bind a question to its source home and audience.</p></div><div><span>02</span><strong>Packet</strong><p>Separate observation, interpretation, and unresolved edges.</p></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Project</strong><p>Render a readable public module with a loss note.</p></div><div><span>04</span><strong>Review</strong><p>Hold the next implementation or release slice for people.</p></div></section>
  <aside class="program-dossier__boundary"><strong>Public boundary</strong><p>EKRP is presented as an application-profile direction. This page does not claim deployed infrastructure, automatic synthesis, or standards adoption.</p></aside>
</section>
